<report>
<line><title>Risk analysis (prospective)</title></line>
<line></line>
<table>
<tr><td></td><td><subtitle>Characteristic factor:</subtitle></td><td></td></tr>
<tr><td><subtitle>Outcome:</subtitle></td><td>Present</td><td>Absent</td></tr>
<tr><td>Positive</td><td><in>a_out</in></td><td><in>b_out</in></td></tr>
<tr><td>Negative</td><td><in>c_out</in></td><td><in>d_out</in></td></tr>
</table>
<line>Risk ratio (relative risk in incidence study) = <in>ratio</in></line>
<line><ci>Approximate (Koopman) <in>pc</in>% confidence interval = <in>koopman_from</in> to <in>koopman_to</in></ci></line>
<line>Approximate power <in>pwr</in></line>
<line></line>
<line>Risk difference = <in>dif</in></line>
<line><ci>Approximate (Miettinen) <in>pc</in>% confidence interval = <in>miettinen_from</in> to <in>miettinen_to</in></ci></line>
<block name="exposure">
<line></line>
<line>Population exposure % = <in>pe</in></line>
<line>Population attributable risk % = <in>par</in></line>
<line><ci>Approximate (Walter) <in>pc</in>% confidence interval = <in>walter_from</in> to <in>walter_to</in></ci></line>
</block>
</report>